{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnRankDegeneracy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnRankDegeneracy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.Wedderburn","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaRows","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.FullRank"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.yLambda_two_not_realisable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.yLambda_two_not_realisable","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnRankDegeneracy.lean#L282-L300","doc":"**`y_λ = 2` is not realisable**, kept from the morning as the coarser\nstatement: it holds at every `λ` with `π_λ = 1`, where `yLambda_forced_one`\ngives the exact value only at `lam0 n`. Both now follow from\n`yLambda_determined`; before `blockDim` was computed, neither did. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.yLambda_forced_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.yLambda_forced_one","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnRankDegeneracy.lean#L262-L280","doc":"**The weight at the supported partition is forced to `1`** — for an\nARBITRARY decomposition on this carrier, not just the witness above.\n\nThis is what closes `qou-luq7`. The morning's version of this file exhibited\n`rankOneWedderburnDim n d`, an instance with `y_λ = 1/d` for every `d ≥ 1`, and\nrecorded that one-parameter family as the freedom surviving item 1. **That\ndefinition can no longer be written**: `blockDim` is not a field, so a witness\ncannot choose `d`, and `rho` must land in `M_{f^λ}(ℚ)` with `f^λ` computed from\n`λ`. The family collapses to its `d = 1` member, which is `rankOneWedderburn`.\n\nSo on this carrier `y_λ` is not merely constrained, it is determined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.rankOne_blockDim_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.rankOne_blockDim_forced","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnRankDegeneracy.lean#L253-L260","doc":"**The block dimension at the supported partition is forced to `1`.**\n\n`lam0 n` is the single column `[1,1,…,1]`, whose only standard tableau fills the\ncolumn in increasing order — so `f^λ = 1`. Since 2026-08-30 `blockDim` is\n`dimHLF ∘ Partition.parts` rather than a field, this is a *computation*, not a\nchoice the witness makes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.rankOne_yLambda_support_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.rankOne_yLambda_support_one","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnRankDegeneracy.lean#L239-L249","doc":"**The witness assigns weight `1` on its supported partition**, where a\ngenuine Ocneanu weight need not be `1`.\n\nRestricted to the support since PR #6097's class change: `y_λ` must now vanish\noff-support, because `block_scaling` is stated against `Matrix.trace (ρ_λ x)`\nand an `AlgHom` cannot be zero there (`ρ_λ 1 = 1`). The previous\nunconditional-in-`λ` form was available only while `chi_lambda` was a free\nfield that could itself vanish. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.rankOne_finrank_ne_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.rankOne_finrank_ne_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnRankDegeneracy.lean#L228-L237","doc":"The dimension invariant the exclusion rests on, stated on its own so the\n`(b)`-scope citation is checkable: the witness carrier is one-dimensional, and\n`H_n(q)` is not, at every `n ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.wedderburnDecomp_does_not_pin_rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.wedderburnDecomp_does_not_pin_rank","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnRankDegeneracy.lean#L217-L226","doc":"**The headline.** At every `n ≥ 2` the class `WedderburnDecomp` is\ninhabited by an algebra that provably **fails** the Hecke rank predicate.\n\nRead the two conjuncts together: inhabiting `WedderburnDecomp` is compatible\nwith `¬ IsHeckeOfFullRank`, so an instance of the former is not evidence that\nthe carrier is `H_n(q)`. The second conjunct is `not_isHeckeOfFullRank_rankOne`\nfrom `QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean`, i.e. the same invariant PR #4857 introduced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.rankOneWedderburn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.rankOneWedderburn","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnRankDegeneracy.lean#L173-L213","doc":"**The degenerate Wedderburn decomposition, at every `n`.**\n\nEvery field is the class's genuine equation, discharged: no `Prop`-variable\nfield, no `True`, no `sorry`. The carrier is `ℚ`, which is `Nontrivial` — so\nthis is a strictly stronger witness than a `PUnit`-style one, and it is not the\n`triv_wedderburn` pattern of `QOU/Mathlib/HeckeAlgebra.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.lam0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.lam0","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnRankDegeneracy.lean#L160-L170","doc":"The all-ones partition `1 + 1 + ⋯ + 1 = n`. Exists at every `n`, which is\nwhat lets the witness below be stated uniformly rather than at one fixed rank. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.rankOneMarkov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RankOneDegeneracy.rankOneMarkov","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnRankDegeneracy.lean#L149-L158","doc":"The Markov trace on the rank-one model: the identity functional on `ℚ`.\nNormalisation, cyclicity and both generator-value axioms hold because every\ngenerator maps to `1` and `ℚ` is commutative. ","signatureChunk":0}]}